 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Whitted-Style Shading with Diffuse/Glossy Materials — Direct Illumination with Shadow Rays
-A simplified variant that computes only diffuse reflectance and ambient lighting, using shadow rays for visibility but omitting recursive reflection tracing [S2, unofficial]. It is chosen for performance-critical applications where only direct lighting is needed. It returns emissive radiance if the material is emissive, otherwise diffuse reflectance [S2, unofficial].
+A simplified variant that computes only diffuse reflectance and ambient lighting, using shadow rays for visibility but omitting recursive reflection tracing [S2, unofficial]. It is chosen for performance-critical applications where only direct lighting is needed [S2, unofficial]. It returns emissive radiance if the material is emissive, otherwise diffuse reflectance [S2, unofficial].
 
 ### Glossy Reflection
-Models reflections on rough surfaces by distributing outgoing rays around the perfect mirror reflection direction, controlled by a shininess exponent $\alpha$ [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen when a sharp but not perfect mirror reflection is desired. The intensity is calculated as $(\max(\mathbf{R} \cdot \mathbf{v}, 0))^\alpha$ [S1, unofficial].
+Models reflections on rough surfaces by distributing outgoing rays around the perfect mirror reflection direction, controlled by a shininess exponent $\alpha$ [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen when a sharp but not perfect mirror reflection is desired [S1, unofficial]. The intensity is calculated as $(\max(\mathbf{R} \cdot \mathbf{v}, 0))^\alpha$ [S1, unofficial].
 
 ### Ray Reflection Tracing
-Traces reflected rays to simulate mirror-like reflections, limited to a maximum recursion depth [G]. It is chosen for scenes requiring accurate mirror reflections. It is limited to 1 bounce in the provided implementation [G].
+Traces reflected rays to simulate mirror-like reflections, limited to a maximum recursion depth [G]. It is chosen for scenes requiring accurate mirror reflections [G]. It is limited to 1 bounce in the provided implementation [G].
 
 ### Water Reflection
-A specific application where water reflects the sky it is under, rather than a static color, making low sun angles optimal for visuals [S5, unofficial]. It is chosen for aquatic environments. Swimming underwater limits sight distance to 34 meters and removes red light [S5, unofficial].
